                USING THE DISC, FORM AND SPEED PAGE DIRECTORIES                
                                                                               
The VIEWTEXT system allows .FRM and .SPD respectively. They   
also show the current number of files held on the FILE CAROUSEL, and although  
the full instructions for using the CAROUSEL are not displayed the FORM and    
SPEED directories are otherwise identical to the PAGE di files with different extensions for each type of    
file. The default extension is .PGE for page files. In order to simplify the   
identification of files two further extensions can be used - .FRM for forms,   
and .SPD for speed pages. The three dirrectory in operation.  
                                                                               
ALL DIRECTORIES - the drive code (A-H) is entered, and any file names present  
on the selected disc which match the directory extension are shown inectories will only show those files     
which have a matching extension. (See sections 7.5 and 8.8 on the preparation  
and use of FORM and SPEED pages).                                              
                                                     groups   
of up to 10 names, together with the date recorded and the string. If no files 
are found the user is prompted for another drive code or to press ESCAPE twice 
to exit back to the MAIN MENU.                                                 
                            
PAGE DIRECTORY - called from the MAIN MENU (function 2). This directory also   
displays the instructions for loading and clearing the FILE CAROUSEL, which is 
fully described in section 6 of the User Guide. This directory wi                                                                              
