SAVING FILES - when the user is prompted for a file name the minimum entry is  
a name with up to 8 characters in upper or lower case ( all names are changed  
by VIEWTEXT to upper case). The file will then be saved on the VIEWTEXT disc   
which is always the default drive (see section 1 of the User Guide), and                      is sent to the modem when the RETURN key is      
                              pressed. The state of this flag will be saved    
                              in the CONFIG file.                              
                      the   
extension will default to .PGE (page file). To save a file on any other drive, 
enter the drive code followed by ":" and then the name. If a the file is not   
a page file, enter the required extension (up to 3 characters).                
                                                              
                                                                               
